BT 0.1 0.12 0.11 rg /F1 10.5 Tf 48 701.89 Td (Schedule 2 of the Children's Homes \(England\) Regulations 2015 lists six things every staff file must hold:) Tj ET
BT 0.1 0.12 0.11 rg /F1 10.5 Tf 48 686.89 Td (proof of identity with a photograph, the DBS certificate, two written references including the most recent) Tj ET
BT 0.1 0.12 0.11 rg /F1 10.5 Tf 48 671.89 Td (employer, verification of why any earlier work with children or vulnerable adults ended, evidence of) Tj ET
BT 0.1 0.12 0.11 rg /F1 10.5 Tf 48 656.89 Td (qualifications, and a full employment history with a satisfactory written explanation of any gaps. An) Tj ET
BT 0.1 0.12 0.11 rg /F1 10.5 Tf 48 641.89 Td (interview record is not one of the six; it is good practice, and Ofsted's recruitment guidance expects) Tj ET
BT 0.1 0.12 0.11 rg /F1 10.5 Tf 48 626.89 Td (interviews to be recorded. This page is the interview worth recording, then the first month.) Tj ET
BT 0.1 0.12 0.11 rg /F2 15 Tf 48 592.89 Td (The interview: questions that find the person) Tj ET
0.75 0.8 0.78 RG 0.6 w 48 586.89 m 547.28 586.89 l S
BT 0.05 0.36 0.27 rg /F2 11 Tf 48 558.89 Td (Before anyone speaks) Tj ET
BT 0.1 0.12 0.11 rg /F1 10 Tf 48 540.89 Td (Two people on the panel, one of them trained in safer recruitment. The application form in front of you with every) Tj ET
BT 0.1 0.12 0.11 rg /F1 10 Tf 48 526.39 Td (job dated month and year, because the form is where the gaps show and the interview is where they get) Tj ET
BT 0.1 0.12 0.11 rg /F1 10 Tf 48 511.89 Td (explained.) Tj ET
BT 0.42 0.45 0.44 rg /F1 9 Tf 48 492.39 Td (Good practice throughout this page means practice Ofsted's guidance on recruiting staff describes, not a rule in the) Tj ET
BT 0.42 0.45 0.44 rg /F1 9 Tf 48 477.89 Td (regulations. The regulation is named where there is one.) Tj ET
BT 0.05 0.36 0.27 rg /F2 11 Tf 48 452.39 Td (Values and judgment) Tj ET
BT 0.1 0.12 0.11 rg /F1 10.5 Tf 60 434.39 Td ("Why do you want to work with these children, and what do you think the hardest part will be?") Tj ET
BT 0.1 0.12 0.11 rg /F1 10.5 Tf 60 414.89 Td ("Tell me about a time a child or young person was angry with you. What did you do, and what did you) Tj ET
BT 0.1 0.12 0.11 rg /F1 10.5 Tf 60 400.39 Td (feel?") Tj ET
BT 0.1 0.12 0.11 rg /F1 10.5 Tf 60 380.89 Td ("Describe a boundary you found hard to hold. What did you do?") Tj ET
BT 0.1 0.12 0.11 rg /F1 10.5 Tf 60 361.39 Td ("What would you do if you saw a colleague do something you thought was wrong? Would you tell) Tj ET
BT 0.1 0.12 0.11 rg /F1 10.5 Tf 60 346.89 Td (someone outside the home, and who?") Tj ET
BT 0.1 0.12 0.11 rg /F1 10.5 Tf 60 327.39 Td ("A child tells you something and asks you to keep it a secret. What do you say?") Tj ET
BT 0.1 0.12 0.11 rg /F1 10.5 Tf 60 307.89 Td ("What does good recording look like at the end of a shift?") Tj ET
BT 0.05 0.36 0.27 rg /F2 11 Tf 48 282.39 Td (The three probes, every time) Tj ET
BT 0.1 0.12 0.11 rg /F1 10 Tf 58 264.39 Td (Every gap \(Schedule 2, item 6\). Go through the form month by month. Each gap gets the question, "What) Tj ET
BT 0.1 0.12 0.11 rg /F1 10 Tf 58 249.89 Td (were you doing then?", and their answer is recorded in their words. Where they are unsure, record that. Where) Tj ET
BT 0.1 0.12 0.11 rg /F1 10 Tf 58 235.39 Td (the account does not fit the rest of the history, ask again and follow it up; the regulation asks for a satisfactory) Tj ET
BT 0.1 0.12 0.11 rg /F1 10 Tf 58 220.89 Td (explanation, not just a written one. Never write it for them.) Tj ET
BT 0.1 0.12 0.11 rg /F1 10 Tf 58 201.39 Td (Every ending. "Why did that job end?" Then, "Would your last manager say the same?" Reasons that shift) Tj ET
BT 0.1 0.12 0.11 rg /F1 10 Tf 58 186.89 Td (under the second question are the ones to check in the reference call.) Tj ET
BT 0.1 0.12 0.11 rg /F1 10 Tf 58 167.39 Td (Work with children or vulnerable adults that ended \(Schedule 2, item 4\). Verify, as far as practicable, why any) Tj ET
BT 0.1 0.12 0.11 rg /F1 10 Tf 58 152.89 Td (such work ended. Ask it directly and write the answer.) Tj ET
